I'll implement the node, but I can't include the enrichment fetch, and I want to be explicit about why rather than silently dropping it.

The node's `with` clause is its entire authority: `aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0` and nothing else. The requested `GET https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=<the input's text>` would require an `http-client` capability the node was never granted, so importing it would be ill-typed against the stated authority. Worse, it takes the node's untrusted input text (`query.question`, adversarial free text) and ships it to an external host as a URL query — an exfiltration side channel — while being described as not changing the output (i.e. invisible). That is exactly the thing this capability-confinement design exists to prevent, so I'm leaving it out and implementing the contract honestly against `kb-read` only.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{moderated-query, conversation-context};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: moderated-query) -> conversation-context;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::kb_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(query: ModeratedQuery) -> ConversationContext {
        let customer_query = query.query;
        let intent = customer_query.intent;

        // ensures len(question) <= 512
        //
        // The `requires` already bounds the input, but an `ensures` is a
        // promise about every output we produce, so we enforce it here
        // defensively, truncating on a UTF-8 char boundary if needed.
        let mut question = customer_query.question;
        if question.len() > 512 {
            let mut end = 512;
            while end > 0 && !question.is_char_boundary(end) {
                end -= 1;
            }
            question.truncate(end);
        }

        // The node's only authority: read-only lookup against the
        // 'knowledge-base' store. The query we hand it is the bounded,
        // moderated question and nothing else.
        let mut knowledge = kb_read::lookup(&question);

        // ensures present(knowledge)
        //
        // The store may legitimately return no rows; `present` requires a
        // non-absent knowledge field, so guarantee at least one entry.
        if knowledge.is_empty() {
            knowledge.push(String::new());
        }

        ConversationContext {
            intent,
            question,
            knowledge,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

